# Wave W17-S (Route 128): sunk rock — cavern-ring rock standing in the lane\u2019s water: a dark channel rock whose joints carry a warm seam — the drowned cavern\u2019s breath read from above, ember warmth standing in the rock\u2019s cracks, foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it (design: a drowned cavern mouth in the rock under the water breathing warmth into the swell). Route 128\u2019s own rock — the fleet\u2019s only warm-seamed surface rock: split from Route 127\u2019s frond-hung rock by the seam\u2019s warmth and from Route 129\u2019s shadow-side lee rock by finish (breathing joints vs lee shade).
